## Renaming connected nodes

Changing a node's name replaces it. CTMS rejects deletion while a route still references the node. Set `lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }` on connected nodes and use resource references for the node IDs in managed routes.
Terraform can then create the node with its new name, update the routes to its new ID, and delete the original node.

The replacement name must be unique. Forcing replacement while retaining the same name can fail because CTMS does not allow two nodes with that name. Routes managed outside this Terraform configuration must be removed or rewired separately before the original node can be deleted.

