## Import

Import is supported using the following syntax:

{{tffile .ImportFile}}
{{- end }}

Alternatively, use a structured identity in an `import` block with Terraform 1.14 or later:

```terraform
import {
  to       = btpservice_ctms_node.source
  provider = btpservice.landscape
  identity = {
    endpoint = "https://transport-service-app-backend.ts.cfapps.eu10.hana.ondemand.com"
    id       = "12345"
  }
}
```

Configure the `btpservice.landscape` provider alias with credentials for the intended CTMS landscape and set `provider = btpservice.landscape` on the destination resource block as well.
Set the identity's `endpoint` to that provider's CTMS service root without `/v2` or a trailing slash.
The regional endpoint may be shared by tenants; the credentials select the landscape.

## Restriction

### Labels of Nodes

The current version of the V2 API for cTMS landscape management (status: 23.11.2026) does not support the creation or modification of labels. Consequently the resource does not comprise these attributes.

### Import-disabled attributes

The managed node resource omits `import_disabled` and `import_disabled_reason` because of gaps in the V2 API's create/update behavior (status: 23.11.2026).
The `btpservice_ctms_node` and `btpservice_ctms_nodes` data sources expose these attributes as read-only values when returned by the API. Other import-related settings, including `auto_import` and deployment `import_options`, remain available on the managed resource.
